  "_signature": "Each block declares the computed values that would be wrong if its stylesheet never shipped, or its rule lost to a broader selector, or its box stopped being the shape that makes it readable as itself. Type AND layout, because three defects in a row were invisible to every other check: a block that renders, counts and aligns can still be the wrong size, the wrong width, or spaced wrong. DECLARED HERE, NOT READ BACK FROM THE CSS: comparing a computed value to the rule that produced it proves only that the browser works. `source` records where each value came from. `expect` holds values asserted at every width; `expectAt` holds the ones that differ by width.",
  "_containment": "Geometry between TWO elements, which no computed value can express. Every value in `signature` describes one box in isolation; a child spilling out of its parent is a relationship. The child's margin box is compared against the parent's PADDING box, so a child that fills its parent edge to edge fails alongside one that overflows."
